.TH CDPREPRUNMKISOFS\-111 1 17/12/98 "CADC"
 
.SH NAME
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111
\- runs \fBmkisofs\fR to create an image of a CD\-ROM on magnetic disk.
 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111 \fIvolume\-name mkiosfsrc\-file\-path log\-file\-path\fR
.I work\-path data\-path
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111
is a C\-shell script that uses \fBmkisofs\fR to create an image of a
CD\-ROM on magnetic disk.
.B mkisofs
is a free software package which creates an ISO9660 file system
with optional Rock Ridge attributes.

This script places all files in the 
.I data\-path
on the magnetic disk image.  It is expected that this directory may
contain hard links to the actual data.

This script was written to work with an application such as
.B cdPrep
or 
.B mediaPrep
which interface with SYBASE.

.SH OPERATION
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111 
requires seven command\-line parameters:
.TP
.I volume\-name:      
Name of disk in upper\-case.
.TP
.I mkiosfsrc\-file\-path: 
Fully specified path and name of mkiosfsrc file.
.TP
.I log\-file\-path:    
Fully specified path and name of log file.
.TP
.I work\-path:   
Fully specified path to the work directory.  This is the location on
magnetic disk where the CD\-ROM image will be created.
.TP
.I data\-path
Fully specified path to the directory which contains the data.
This directory may contain the data or hard links to the real data.

.SH OPTIONS
There are no optional command\-line arguments for
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111
 
.SH USAGE
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111
should not require any operator input.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP 3
The following example demonstrates how to use
.B cdPrepRunMkisofs
.RS 5
.sp 1n
.nf
.BR "example% cdPrepRunMkisofs " ARCH4_0202 " " /dot_files/mkisofsrc " " /logs/cdPrep
.BR "        " /staging/media/staging2 " " /staging/archive/staging2
.sp 1n
.fi
.RE
.RS 3
In this example copies of volume (unit) 
.B ARCH4_0202
will be created in
.I /staging/media/staging2.
The configuration file is located at
.I /dot_files/mkisofsrc
and the log file is located
at
.I /logs/cdPrep.
The data can be found in
.I /staging/arcvhie/staging2
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
The shell's path variable
should include the locations of the 
.B mkisofs
executable.
 
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B cdPrepRunMkiosfs\-111
returns a 0 to the calling environment upon successful completion.
Otherwise a non\-zero number is returned. 
 
